{
  "title": "Amazon Macie to AWS Step Functions to Amazon S3 Quarantine",
  "description": "Automated sensitive data response: Amazon Macie findings trigger AWS Step Functions to classify severity and quarantine objects in Amazon S3",
  "language": "TypeScript",
  "level": "300",
  "framework": "AWS CDK",
  "introBox": {
    "headline": "How it works",
    "text": [
      "This pattern deploys an automated sensitive data response pipeline.",
      "Amazon Macie scans Amazon S3 objects for sensitive data and publishes findings to Amazon EventBridge.",
      "An Amazon EventBridge rule triggers an AWS Step Functions state machine that classifies findings by severity.",
      "High-severity findings result in automatic object quarantine (moved to a separate Amazon S3 bucket).",
      "Medium-severity findings result in object tagging with finding metadata.",
      "All findings trigger Amazon SNS notifications to the security team."
    ]
  },
